	 *
	 * - The comparison sign is inverted when both sides of the inequality are
	 *   multiplied/divided by a negative number, so if `one < 0` the comparison
	 *   needs to be flipped.
	 * - `INT64_MAX / -1` itself overflows (or traps), so that case should be
	 *   avoided.
